license: "MIT"

abstract: >
  This repository contains the code for FlexLMV-Net, 
  a longitudinal multi-view deep learning model for breast cancer risk prediction. 
  FlexLMV-Net jointly models complementary CC and MLO mammographic views while incorporating 
  a variable number of prior examinations, allowing the model to adapt to patients with 
  different amounts of available longitudinal imaging. 
  It uses explicit temporal alignment, temporal feature fusion, dual-stream attention, 
  and multi-view learning to capture longitudinal changes and complementary information 
  between mammographic views. The model is evaluated on the EMBED and CSAW-CC datasets and 
  demonstrates improved breast cancer risk prediction across follow-up years, breast density categories, 
  and cancer subgroups. The repository provides preprocessing, training, inference, and 
  evaluation pipelines to facilitate reproducible research and comparison with existing breast 
  cancer risk prediction methods.